.TH MICROVM-MCP-INSTALL-IMAGE 1 "September 2026" "microvm-mcp" "Administrator Commands"
.SH NAME
microvm-mcp-install-image \- install a digest-pinned guest image bundle
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B microvm-mcp-install-image --image-id
.I ID
.B --rootfs
.I FILE
.B --rootfs-sha256
.I DIGEST
.B --kernel
.I FILE
.B --kernel-sha256
.I DIGEST
.RB [ --state-dir
.IR DIRECTORY ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copies trusted local guest artifacts into a new images/ID directory on the
state volume. Requires root. Checks both SHA-256 digests and reflink support
between the installed rootfs and state directory before publishing the bundle.
The default state directory is /var/lib/microvm-mcp.
.PP
Existing image bundles are not overwritten. The command prints an
[images.ID] TOML table for the operator to add to /etc/microvm-mcp.toml; one
configured image must be marked default = true. It does not edit configuration
or start the service. Guest code is not executed by this installer.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the bundle was installed. Nonzero means installation failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR microvm-mcp (1)
